    <description>The short-lived arms dealer VnS attempted to break into the automatic squad weaponry market with the Scylla, a three barrel rotary 12.7 x 99 mm cartridge heavy machine gun platform. It is more accurate and devastating than the StA 3, but has crippling flaws in weight, a slow reload, and extreme expense, costing as much as three StA-3's. As a mounted HMG, the weapon becomes noticeably more accurate, making it fairly common at static frontline helghan command posts and trenches.</description>
