  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseArtilleryWeapon">
    <defName>Artillery_HG_AutoMortar</defName>
    <label>StA-120 A.M.S Gorgon (Gun)</label>
    <description>Before the development of the StA-X3 Helghan artillery crews struggled to find a suitable weapon for mid to small range engagements. The Gorgon was proposed reluctantly as a temporary measure, developed as a local installation for fixed defensive positions with promises made to render it self-propelled 'at a future time'. The gorgon was not called that originally- its a derogatory term thought up by frontline units forced to service the 'ugly, dangerous' construction, which had a habit of mangling limbs of maintenance crews and generally appeared to be 'ugly' to many garrison units. The Gorgon's unique odd 'stilt' support tower was likely recycled- either from old water towers or orbital defense guns, repurposed to raise the turrets main gun up, a 'heavy mortar' light field gun, in order to get better firing angles without needing to carve into civilian buildings.\n\nThey were especially common around Salamun district in Pyrrhus, in set hidden killzones to harass high traffic areas as part of Radec's defense plan. The key feature of the gorgon is that once set, a central firing computer can run the gun autonomously, meaning local troops need only defend its exposed infrastructure. In ideal circumstances, Gorgons would be built into bunker complexes, covering the relatively weak support structure, exposing only the robust cannon itself on the roof. In reality during the siege of Pyrrhus these were set up in scattered urban sectors to optimize lines of fire and obscure them until it was time to strike.</description>
    <recoilPower>2</recoilPower>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Helghast/Structures/Turrets/TurretGorgon_Top</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <weaponTags>
      <li>Artillery_BaseDestroyer</li>
    </weaponTags>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Verb_Shoot</verbClass>
		<defaultProjectile>Bullet_Shell_HighExplosive</defaultProjectile>
        <forceNormalTimeSpeed>false</forceNormalTimeSpeed>
        <warmupTime>4.0</warmupTime>
        <forcedMissRadius>7</forcedMissRadius>
        <forcedMissRadiusClassicMortars>7</forcedMissRadiusClassicMortars>
        <isMortar>true</isMortar>
        <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
        <minRange>39.9</minRange>
        <range>750</range>
        <burstShotCount>1</burstShotCount>
        <soundCast>Mortar_LaunchA</soundCast>
        <muzzleFlashScale>16</muzzleFlashScale>
        <consumeFuelPerShot>1</consumeFuelPerShot>
        <targetParams>
          <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
        </targetParams>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
